---
/**
 * Chapter 3's input-billing ladder: one prompt, one stage per row, with the
 * operator riding on the arrow between two stages.
 *
 * It appears TWICE — as the second fragment of the vocabulary slide's right
 * panel (where the room has just watched the same prompt become 1,240 tokens)
 * and as the right column of the credits slide (where the rates are on the
 * wall next to it). It is a component so the two can never drift apart.
 *
 * Text lives here; every figure is written in by the deck's controller from
 * src/lib/asml-ai/rates.ts, into EVERY copy on the page.
 */
---

<ol class="bill-ladder">
  <li class="st">
    <span class="lab">your prompt</span>
    <span class="quote"
      >&ldquo;Summarise last week&rsquo;s throughput report and flag anything
      unusual.&rdquo;</span
    >
    <span class="sub">+ the 4-page report you attached</span>
  </li>
  <li class="op"><i>counted &mdash; roughly chars &divide; 4</i></li>
  <li class="st">
    <b class="n" data-bill-tokens>0</b>
    <span class="lab">input tokens</span>
  </li>
  <li class="op"><i data-bill-rate></i></li>
  <li class="st">
    <b class="n" data-bill-aic>0</b>
    <span class="lab">AI credits</span>
  </li>
  <li class="op"><i>1 AIC = 1 US cent, &divide; 1.08</i></li>
  <li class="st last">
    <b class="n" data-bill-eur>&euro;0.00</b>
    <span class="lab">what it cost</span>
  </li>
</ol>
